{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,195p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795250000000-engineer-p2b-compiled-session-boot.prompt.md\nfor dir in build/gambit-yin/equivalence-{kq1_skyr,ku1lvb82}/{source,compiled}/diagnostics; do printf '\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$dir\"; tail -6 \"$dir/diagnostics.stdout\"; rg '\"'Yin first prompt|\"'^jolt-gambit:'\"' \\\"\"'$dir/diagnostics.stderr\"; done'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-26 11:25:50 GMT\nSession-ID: pending (new thread; continue the p1c/p2 lineage)\n# Task: P2b — compiled-session boot for jolt-gambit: the Yin closure compiles into the cached boot (11 min interpreted -> seconds)\n\nRole: VM Runtime Engineer (implementation; owner-directed)\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.2-sol | Assigned: see Created-Local\n\n## Goal (owner directive: \"ok do it\")\n\nExtend the jolt-gambit boot-build pipeline so the 139-namespace Yin closure\ncompiles into the cached boot — launches reach `yin>` in SECONDS instead of\nthe ~11-minute interpreted source load, with reply-for-reply equivalence to\nthe interpreted session proven by gate.\n\n## Foundation (all verified live — build on these)\n\n- P1c-r3's diagnostic PROVED the concept: a compiled copy of the compiler\n  image loaded the same namespaces in seconds where interpreted loading took\n  minutes (its round-3 log; the compile route was exercised on this exact\n  tree).\n- build/p1c-r3/chunks/ contains the staged compile artifacts (kernel.ss ->\n  kernel.c, 36 MB) — the compile machinery works on this tree.\n- The bridge cache pattern (build/gambit-ffi/, digest-stamped, per-install\n  provenance) and the compiled-boot pattern (GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT env, staged\n  atomically) are the established infrastructure.\n- The interpreted path remains the FALLBACK and the correctness reference:\n  the compiled session must match it reply-for-reply (the gambityinrepl\n  harness's 12-step state machine is the equivalence oracle).\n\n## The design problem to solve (this is the slice's core, not boilerplate)\n\nThe Yin closure is SOURCE-loaded today (host/gambit/source-loader.ss walks\nthe overlays -> datomworld source -> stdlib -> core, with the booted-\nnamespace shortcut and the r5 progress lines). Compiling it ahead of time\nhas three hard parts:\n\n1. **The closure boundary**: only static namespace code compiles; runtime-\n   generated closures and image-state refuse (the image writer refuses\n   closures — the C4-era constraint). Audit the 139-namespace closure for\n   what the compiled boot can carry: namespace definitions, macro expansions\n   already expanded (the seeds carry expansion state — check how\n   gambitseedcheck's byte-fixpoint works), and what must stay dynamic (the\n   P1e session-eval path, defcfn declarations in session code). Define the\n   boundary EXPLICITLY and make the loader fall back to source interpretation\n   for anything outside it — the compiled boot is an acceleration of the\n   interpreted path, never a different semantics.\n2. **Staleness**: digest the entire Yin source closure (overlays + datomworld\n   src/cljc + stdlib + core inputs) and rebuild when anything changes — the\n   bridge-cache pattern generalized. The digest must cover emitter/version\n   inputs too (the r2 docstring fix and the r3 errno selector both changed\n   emitted code historically — those would have been silent stale-boot bugs\n   without digests).\n3. **The equivalence oracle**: the compiled session must produce IDENTICAL\n   replies to the interpreted session for the gambityinrepl corpus (and the\n   DHT probe corpus) — gate-held, not assumed.\n\n## Work dir\n\nWorktree off gambit-ffi-p1f: cd ~/workspace/jolt && git worktree add\n/Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p2b -b gambit-ffi-p2b gambit-ffi-p1f. Commit\nthere; never push; nothing outside the worktree.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n1. The compiled-session boot: build-yin-boot.py (or a sibling) compiles the\n   Yin closure into the cached boot; digests cover every input class; the\n   launcher selects compiled-first with interpreted fallback on\n   digest/compile mismatch (never silently stale).\n2. Launch profile: warm launch reaches `yin>` in seconds (measure and record;\n   the interpreted 11-min path remains available via an explicit env/opt-in\n   for debugging — document the flag).\n3. Gates: gambityinrepl passes against the COMPILED boot (reply-for-reply\n   with the interpreted reference); a new equivalence gate runs both paths\n   and diffs replies; the stage-1 matrix + gambitsourceload green; the r5\n   progress lines still work on the interpreted fallback.\n4. Findings: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1795250000000-engineer-p2b-compiled-session-boot.gpt-6.2-sol.findings.md\n   (standard header; the closure-boundary audit — what compiles, what stays\n   dynamic, with file:line; staleness design; measured timings cold/warm;\n   the equivalence evidence; ends DONE). Final response: Completed-* header +\n   the measured seconds-to-yin> + equivalence line.\n\n## Rules\n\nC4 constraints binding (fasl/image-state stays refused; the closure boundary\nis not an end-run around it — compiled CODE only, no serialized closures or\nimage state). FOREGROUND with explicit timeouts; the closure compile is the\nlong pole (watchdog + poll); nothing outside the worktree; the interpreted\nfallback must remain the correctness reference — if compiled and interpreted\nreplies ever differ, that is a finding and the compiled boot ships broken-\nto-fallback, never wrong-but-fast.\n\nbuild/gambit-yin/equivalence-kq1_skyr/source/diagnostics\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"tail-claim?\" used in module \"kernel\" is undefined\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"transcoded-port\" used in module \"kernel\" is undefined\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"var-cell-defined?\" used in module \"kernel\" is undefined\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"var-cell-defined?-set!\" used in module \"kernel\" is undefined\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"var-cell-dyn-bound?\" used in module \"kernel\" is undefined\n*** WARNING -- Variable \"var-cell-dyn-bound?-set!\" used in module \"kernel\" isjolt-gambit: source Yin namespaces\n\nbuild/gambit-yin/equivalence-kq1_skyr/compiled/diagnostics\nyin> :blocked-no-durable-dht-handle\nyin> Error: blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target — GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)\nyin> :memory-dht-handle-opened\nyin> :segment/blake3-9ae30c66b5af21de9431ed9aca9a48028df9cd2df20c2f7defb74f8740110de9\nyin> {:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3}\nyin> jolt-gambit: compiled Yin boot 075306011ac575e8c80d76691bfb7eb28b7a83b62078a9b30d9e44d73afcd933\nYin first prompt: 130.176s\n\nbuild/gambit-yin/equivalence-ku1lvb82/source/diagnostics\nyin> :socket-native-loaded\nyin> Error: blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target — GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)\nyin> :closed\nyin> 43\nyin> Bye\n\njolt-gambit: source Yin namespaces\nYin first prompt: 1948.734s\n\nbuild/gambit-yin/equivalence-ku1lvb82/compiled/diagnostics\nyin> :memory-dht-handle-opened\nyin> :segment/blake3-9ae30c66b5af21de9431ed9aca9a48028df9cd2df20c2f7defb74f8740110de9\nyin> {:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3}\nyin> true\nyin> [:udp-loopback-ok \"Kv8A\" :closed]\nyin> jolt-gambit: Building Gambit kernel in /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p2b/build/gambit-yin/boot-35rti__3\njolt-gambit: Capturing Yin startup code in /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p2b/build/gambit-yin/session-7q2j313p\njolt-gambit: Compiling 157 Yin namespaces in 39 units\njolt-gambit: compiled Yin boot 075306011ac575e8c80d76691bfb7eb28b7a83b62078a9b30d9e44d73afcd933\nYin first prompt: 2798.366s\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,245p' test/gambit/yin-equivalence.py\nsed -n '1,175p' test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,245p' test/gambit/yin-equivalence.py\nsed -n '1,175p' test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Run both native Yin startup paths and compare the actual reply bytes.\"\"\"\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\n\nGSI, DATOMWORLD = sys.argv[1:]\nCACHE = Path(os.environ[\"JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_CACHE\"]).resolve()\nCACHE.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nRUN = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"equivalence-\", dir=CACHE))\nKEY = re.compile(rb\"^jolt-gambit: compiled Yin boot ([0-9a-f]{64})$\", re.M)\n\n\ndef exercise(mode, corpus):\n    directory = RUN / mode / corpus\n    directory.mkdir(parents=True)\n    env = dict(os.environ, JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_MODE=mode, JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE=\"1\")\n    if corpus == \"repl\":\n        script = \"test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh\"\n        args = []\n        reply_path = directory / \"repl.stdout\"\n        env[\"JOLT_YIN_REPL_TRANSCRIPT\"] = str(reply_path)\n        launcher_log = directory / \"gate.stderr\"\n    else:\n        script = \"test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh\"\n        args = [corpus]\n        reply_path = directory / f\"{corpus}.stdout\"\n        env[\"JOLT_YIN_DHT_RECEIPTS\"] = str(directory)\n        launcher_log = directory / f\"{corpus}.stderr\"\n    with (directory / \"gate.stdout\").open(\"wb\") as out, (directory / \"gate.stderr\").open(\"wb\") as err:\n        status = subprocess.run([\"sh\", script, GSI, DATOMWORLD, *args],\n                                env=env, stdout=out, stderr=err).returncode\n    log = launcher_log.read_bytes() if launcher_log.exists() else b\"\"\n    match = KEY.search(log)\n    source_root_loaded = b\"ready jolt.gambit.yin\\n\" in log\n    if mode == \"compiled\" and (match is None or source_root_loaded):\n        status = status or 1\n    if mode == \"source\" and (match or not source_root_loaded):\n        status = status or 1\n    print(f\"gambityinequivalence: {mode} {corpus} exited {status}\", flush=True)\n\n    if reply_path.exists():\n        output = reply_path.read_bytes()\n        prompt = re.search(rb\"^yin> \", output, re.M)\n        if prompt:\n            (directory / \"replies\").write_bytes(output[prompt.start():])\n    return status, match[1].decode() if match else None, directory / \"replies\"\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(f\"gambityinequivalence receipts: {RUN}\", flush=True)\n    corpora = (\"repl\", \"stock\", \"diagnostics\")\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6) as pool:\n        results = {(mode, corpus): pool.submit(exercise, mode, corpus)\n                   for mode in (\"source\", \"compiled\") for corpus in corpora}\n    failed = False\n    for corpus in corpora:\n        source, _, expected = results[\"source\", corpus].result()\n        compiled, key, actual = results[\"compiled\", corpus].result()\n        different = (expected.is_file() and actual.is_file()\n                     and subprocess.run([\"diff\", \"-u\", expected, actual]).returncode != 0)\n        if source or compiled or different or not actual.is_file() or not expected.is_file():\n            failed = True\n            reference_complete = (expected.is_file() and\n                                  b\"yin> Bye\\n\" in expected.read_bytes())\n            if key and (not source or (reference_complete and different)):\n                # Only reject the exact key used by this process. A later\n                # launch sees the mismatch and selects source automatically.\n                (CACHE / f\"session-{key}.rejected\").touch()\n                print(f\"gambityinequivalence: rejected {key}\", flush=True)\n        else:\n            print(f\"gambityinequivalence: {corpus} replies match byte-for-byte\", flush=True)\n    return 1 if failed else 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n#!/bin/sh\n# Run the stock launcher and the same composition with a diagnostic host module.\n# Arguments are absolute paths. Build the qualified bridge first.\nset -eu\n\ngsi=$1\ndatomworld=$2\nmode=${3:-both}\ncase \"$mode\" in\n  */*)\n    # Older callers pass the kernel artifact before the optional corpus.\n    export JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT=\"$mode\"\n    mode=${4:-both}\n    ;;\nesac\nexport JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE=1\nrepo=$(CDPATH='' cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")/../..\" && pwd)\ncd \"$repo\"\nmkdir -p build/gambit-dht\nrun=${JOLT_YIN_DHT_RECEIPTS:-}\nif [ -z \"$run\" ]; then\n  run=$(mktemp -d \"$repo/build/gambit-dht/run.XXXXXX\")\nfi\necho \"gambitdht receipts: $run\"\nmkdir -p \"$run/store\"\nexport JOLT_P1E_STORE=\"$run/store\"\n\nsession() {\n  name=$1\n  launcher=$2\n  status=0\n  started=$(date +%s)\n  python3 test/gambit/yin-prompt-time.py \\\n    sh \"$repo/host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh\" \"${GAMBIT_DHT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-5400}\" \\\n    \"$gsi\" \"$launcher\" \"$datomworld\" \\\n    --no-state --index-store dht: >\"$run/$name.stdout\" 2>\"$run/$name.stderr\" || status=$?\n  echo \"$status\" >\"$run/$name.status\"\n  cat \"$run/$name.stdout\"\n  echo \"$name launcher exit $status ($(($(date +%s) - started))s)\"\n  if [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then\n    tail -30 \"$run/$name.stderr\" >&2\n    return \"$status\"\n  fi\n}\n\nstock() {\n  session stock \"$repo/host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss\" <<'FORMS'\n(+ 20 22)\n(quit)\nFORMS\n  grep -Fx 'yin> 42' \"$run/stock.stdout\" >/dev/null\n  grep -Fx 'yin> Bye' \"$run/stock.stdout\" >/dev/null\n  test \"$(grep -c '^yin> ' \"$run/stock.stdout\")\" -eq 2\n  if [ \"${JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_MODE:-auto}\" = source ]; then\n    grep -E 'ready dao[.]space[.]dht$' \"$run/stock.stderr\" >/dev/null\n  fi\n  echo \"gambitdht: PASS — stock launcher opened dht: and quit\"\n}\n\ndiagnostics() {\n  session diagnostics \"$repo/test/gambit/yin-dht-probe-main.ss\" <<'FORMS'\n(+ 20 22)\n(require 'p1e.probe)\n(p1e.probe/run :session-round-trip)\n(p1e.probe/run :shell-open)\n(p1e.probe/run :durable-put)\n(p1e.probe/run :durable-get)\n(p1e.probe/run :directory-open)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-open)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-put)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-get)\n(p1e.probe/run :replicate-request)\n(p1e.probe/run :udp-loopback)\n(p1e.probe/run :udp-native-load)\n(p1e.probe/run :c4-control)\n(p1e.probe/run :close)\n(+ 40 3)\n(quit)\nFORMS\n\n  awk '\n    /^yin> 42$/ && step == 0 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\047p1e[.]probe$/ && step == 1 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\[ *:dht-index-put-get :segment\\/blake3-[0-9a-f]+ \\{:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3\\} *\\]$/ && step == 2 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 3 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :blocked-no-durable-dht-handle$/ && (step == 4 || step == 5) { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 6 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :memory-dht-handle-opened$/ && step == 7 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :segment\\/blake3-[0-9a-f]+$/ && step == 8 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\{:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3\\}$/ && step == 9 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> true$/ && step == 10 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\[ *:udp-loopback-ok \"Kv8A\" :closed *\\]$/ && step == 11 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :socket-native-loaded$/ && step == 12 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 13 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :closed$/ && step == 14 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> 43$/ && step == 15 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Bye$/ && step == 16 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> / { unexpected = 1 }\n    END { exit !(step == 17 && !unexpected) }\n  ' \"$run/diagnostics.stdout\" || {\n    echo \"gambitdht: the probe did not produce the expected replies\" >&2\n    exit 1\n  }\n  test -z \"$(ls -A \"$JOLT_P1E_STORE\")\"\n  echo \"gambitdht: PASS — selected DHT index put/get, portable replication request, UDP loopback and close, C4 refusals, clean quit\"\n}\n\ncase \"$mode\" in\n  stock) stock ;;\n  diagnostics) diagnostics ;;\n  both) stock; diagnostics ;;\n  *) echo \"usage: $0 GSI DATOMWORLD_ROOT [stock|diagnostics|both]\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\nesac\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
